  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust boundaries",
      "items": [
        "Service edge: every call except /healthz needs an Entra ID token with notifications.send (scp, scope or roles)",
        "Microsoft 365 tenant: the Graph sender signs in as its own mail-sender app, never the API's registration",
        "Mail.Send is scoped to the one sending mailbox with RBAC for Applications",
        "Callers name a Teams destination, never a URL"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One email sender",
      "items": [
        "Sender = Smtp (default) or Graph; only the selected sender is created",
        "A missing sender setting: start-up warning, email ends Skipped (ChannelNotConfigured)",
        "Graph saves each mail to the mailbox's Sent Items"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Accept, then deliver",
      "items": [
        "The API validates and renders from the in-image template catalogue, writes the status pending, publishes to the Redis delivery list, then answers 200",
        "Unsupported or unconfigured channel: 200, warning log, status failed, nothing sent",
        "Full list: 503 with Retry-After 30; the limit is for the whole service",
        "GET /v1/notifications/{id} reads pending, success or failed, for the caller's own notifications only"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Best effort, survives a restart",
      "items": [
        "Retries: 5 s then 30 s, at most 3 attempts; a 429 waits for Retry-After, at most 60 s. A retry goes back to the Redis list with a not-before time, never held in memory",
        "The Graph token request is part of the attempt",
        "A deploy or restart loses no waiting notification; a hard crash can lose the 1 message a replica holds; no database"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Settings and secrets",
      "items": [
        "One set of channel settings per deployment",
        "SMTP password, Graph client secret and webhook URLs: environment variables or Azure App Configuration",
        "Graph with workload identity holds no secret",
        "Local run: Aspire AppHost with Redis and Mailpit, Sender = Smtp"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Client package",
      "items": [
        "DKNet.Notification.Client runs inside the caller's process; it is not a component of this service",
        "Refit methods for POST and GET /v1/notifications; nothing for /healthz",
        "The caller's own DelegatingHandler adds the Entra ID token; every refusal is one exception type"
      ]
    }
  ]
